# 12-Bar Blues Shuffle in E, quick change (repertoire plan: st-blues-shuffle-e). An original study
# on the traditional 12-bar form with the quick change: E A E E | A A E E | B7 A E B7, played
# twice, then a last E7. The shuffle is the one from st-blues-shuffle-a, moved to E: the open
# string 6 (E) with string 5 fret 2 (B), then with string 5 fret 4 (C#); for A the same shape one
# string toward string 1, the open string 5 (A) with string 4 fret 2 (E) and fret 4 (F#). Finger 1
# stays on fret 2 and finger 3 reaches fret 4. Bars 9 and 12 strum B7 (x21202) in the same
# long-short swing, down on the beat and up on the short note. Swung eighths are written as
# triplets: a long note (q3, two thirds of the beat) and a short one (e3, the last third).
title: 12-Bar Blues Shuffle in E (quick change)
